      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "πλὴν γινώσκετε πάντες πάντων ὑμῶν πλεῖον κάμνοντα τὸν ἐπίσκοπον",
          "english_quote": "Nevertheless, all of you know that the bishop toils more than all of you",
          "issue": "The main text chooses indicative γινώσκετε, asserting the hearers’ existing knowledge. The form also permits an imperative, asking everyone to recognize the bishop’s greater toil; that reading has substantial contextual support in this sequence of directives. The indicative is defensible, but this material difference between assertion and exhortation is not disclosed.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a note preserving the imperative alternative and explaining the contextual reason for choosing the indicative. Alternatively, provisionally render “Nevertheless, all of you should recognize that the bishop toils more than all of you,” with the indicative alternative noted. Any changed main text requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "πάντων ὑμῶν πλεῖον κάμνοντα τὸν ἐπίσκοπον",
          "english_quote": "The accusative-infinitive construction presents the bishop as bearing greater wearisome labor than every individual hearer.",
          "issue": "The lexical note incorrectly identifies an accusative–infinitive construction. There is no infinitive here: κάμνοντα is an accusative participle agreeing with τὸν ἐπίσκοπον. This does not invalidate the English main text, but it makes the supporting grammatical explanation inaccurate.",
          "suggested_revision": "Correct the note to describe γινώσκετε with the accusative τὸν ἐπίσκοπον and its supplementary or predicative participle κάμνοντα. Preserve the comparison expressed by πάντων ὑμῶν πλεῖον without claiming an infinitival construction.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
