      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ζωοποιοὺς λόγους ἀγνοῶν καὶ ἐκκλησίας κανόνα. οὐκ εἰδὼς",
          "english_quote": "ignorant of life-giving words and the church’s rule and without knowledge",
          "issue": "The draft makes both ζωοποιοὺς λόγους and ἐκκλησίας κανόνα objects of ἀγνοῶν, then takes οὐκ εἰδώς absolutely as “without knowledge.” That construction is defensible, but the notes omit the more straightforward alternative attachment: ζωοποιοὺς λόγους belongs to ἀγνοῶν, while ἐκκλησίας κανόνα belongs to οὐκ εἰδώς. The existing discussion of negation scope does not disclose this separate object-attachment question. The alternative also preserves the source’s distinct formulations for ignorance more transparently. This is interpretive uncertainty, not evidence of source corruption.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add the alternative “ignorant of life-giving words and not knowing the church’s rule” and explain why the main text instead groups both objects under ἀγνοῶν and leaves οὐκ εἰδώς absolute. Explicitly compare that source-transparent alternative with the current wording. If adopting it, a provisional full formulation is “when he learns that after me it was not an unlearned man—ignorant of life-giving words and not knowing the church’s rule—who was entrusted with the teacher’s chair.” Retain disclosure of the printed period and the existing negation-scope alternatives; the proposed replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
